  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the traced flow and root cause:\n\n**1. FastAPI body param solving:** `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py::solve_dependencies` calls `request_body_to_args()`, which for each body `ModelField` calls `field.validate(value, values, loc=loc)`. That `ModelField.validate` shim lives in `fastapi/_compat.py` and, under Pydantic v2, invokes the field's `TypeAdapter`/model `validate_python`/`model_validate_json` path \u2014 this is the FastAPI\u2192Pydantic v2 integration boundary.\n\n**2. Pydantic v2 discriminated-union resolution:** schema construction happens in `pydantic/_internal/_generate_schema.py`, where `apply_model_validators()` wraps a model's core schema with any `@model_validator` decorators \u2014 `mode='before'` validators get applied as the **outermost** layer (`mode == 'outer'`) around the model's `model-fields`/`model` schema, producing a `function-before` core schema node. Separately, `pydantic/_internal/_discriminated_union.py::apply_discriminator`/`_ApplyInferredDiscriminator` converts the `Union[...]` schema into a `tagged-union` schema: it walks each variant's schema to infer the literal discriminator values (`_infer_discriminator_values_for_choice`), tolerating a `function-before` wrapper only via `is_function_with_inner_schema` (from `_core_utils.py`) so it can recurse past it \u2014 but critically, **the tagged-union discriminator lookup itself operates directly on the raw input dict at validation time**, checking for the tag key before ever invoking a chosen variant's schema (or its before-validator).\n\n**3. The bug:** the customer's `model_validator(mode='before')` is on the **container model that owns the discriminated-union field**, not on a union variant. Per `apply_model_validators`, an outer `mode='before'` validator runs first and receives/returns the raw input dict for the whole model, then that (possibly rebuilt) dict is what `model-fields` validation \u2014 including the tagged-union field \u2014 sees. If that before-validator reconstructs the dict (e.g. filtering/renaming keys) and drops the discriminator-bearing key for the union field, the field never reaches `tagged_union_schema`'s discriminator lookup at all. Because the union field itself has a default (`= None`) in the v2 model (common after the v1\u2192v2 port), a missing key is treated as \"field not provided\" rather than \"field invalid\" \u2014 so `model-fields` silently applies the default instead of raising a `missing`/`union_tag_not_found` error. Result: 200 OK, field silently `None`, no 422 \u2014 the discriminator resolution logic in `_discriminated_union.py` is never reached because the key was stripped one layer up, at the outer `before` hook that FastAPI's `request_body_to_args` \u2192 `model_validate_json` chain invokes before any union-specific validation runs.",
